From 4ec9f436bf2e7382fb5bb5233db444b46dd9109e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nova <361320585+q2-nova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:50:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Skip HALMAC message formatting when debug output is compiled
 out

_halmac_msg_print formatted every HALMAC trace with vsnprintf before
discarding it: without CONFIG_RTW_DEBUG every RTW_* output macro is empty
and DBG_MSG_FILTER is unset. HALMAC traces from per-frame paths; on the Q2
the formatting was 16% of the driver transmit thread's cycles (perf,
2026-11-18).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hal/hal_halmac.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hal/hal_halmac.c b/hal/hal_halmac.c
index ff55890..1da1085 100755
--- a/hal/hal_halmac.c
+++ b/hal/hal_halmac.c
@@ -520,6 +520,12 @@ static u8 _halmac_msg_print(void *p, u32 msg_type, u8 msg_level, s8 *fmt, ...)
 		return ret;
 #endif
 
+#ifndef CONFIG_RTW_DEBUG
+	/* Every output below compiles to nothing without CONFIG_RTW_DEBUG;
+	 * HALMAC traces from per-frame paths, so do not format for nothing. */
+	return ret;
+#endif
+
 	str[0] = '\n';
 	va_start(args, fmt);
 	err = vsnprintf(str, MSG_LEN, fmt, args);
-- 
2.56.0

